---
const steps = [
  {
    n: '01',
    t: 'Download the framework',
    d: 'Start with the free 22-page guide. It contains the actual pre-trade checklist we require of members — not a teaser for it.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    t: 'We review your profile',
    d: 'Platform, instruments, account size, and experience. If our tools are wrong for how you trade, we will say so rather than sell you a seat.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    t: 'Cohort onboarding',
    d: 'If a seat opens, you get the indicator package for your platform, a one-to-one setup session, and access to the weekly model notes.',
  },
] as const;
---

<section id="how" class="scroll-mt-20 py-20 lg:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 lg:px-8">
    <p class="eyebrow text-omega-400">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-white lg:text-5xl">Three steps, and a real no</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
      Access is capped because onboarding is done by a person and because edge decays as
      more accounts act on the same reading. That is the whole reason for the invitation
      model.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-12 divide-y divide-white/8 border-y border-white/8">
      {
        steps.map((s) => (
          <li class="grid grid-cols-[3.25rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-4 py-6">
            <span class="display text-2xl text-omega-500">{s.n}</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{s.t}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">{s.d}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
